WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.069
It wasn't so long ago that Larry the Cable
Guy, born Dan Whitney, seemed to be everywhere.

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:08.710
As part of the Blue Collar Comedy Tour, he
entertained millions at stand-up gigs with

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:11.350
his down-home comedy and catchphrases like:

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.090
"Get er done!"

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:12.730
...and...

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.580
"I don’t care who you are, that’s funny
right there!"

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:20.250
He starred in a string of big-screen comedies,
including Delta Farce, Witless Protection,

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.510
and the confusingly titled Larry the Cable
Guy: Health Inspector.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:27.980
"Name's Larry, and I'm the Health Inspector!"

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:32.340
He's also released 10 albums, including the
platinum-certified The Right to Bare Arms.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.539
He even had his own travelogue show, Only
in America, and was the subject of a Comedy

00:00:36.539 --> 00:00:37.839
Central roast.

00:00:37.839 --> 00:00:39.489
But what's become of Larry lately?

00:00:39.489 --> 00:00:41.399
If you've missed him, you're not alone.

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:44.820
But he's actually been plenty busy — just
not in the ways you might think.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.050
Here's what he's been up to.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.629
Pixar superstar

00:00:47.629 --> 00:00:52.629
Larry is a superstar in Pixar land, having
lent his voice to the Cars franchise's Mater,

00:00:52.629 --> 00:00:56.510
the dim-witted, buck-toothed, kind-hearted
tow truck who becomes the best friend of famous

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.100
race car Lightning McQueen.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.379
Mater was the breakout character of the first
Cars, a box office smash, so he and Larry

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:03.879
were the focus of Cars 2.

00:01:03.879 --> 00:01:08.080
The plot: Mater inadvertently becomes a James
Bond-style international spy.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:09.990
You can probably guess how that went…

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:12.540
"Hey computer, make me a German truck!"

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:13.540
"Request acknowledged!"

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.450
"Check it out, I’m wearing Materhosen.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.670
Make me a monster truck!"

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:17.660
"Request acknowledged!"

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:18.200
"What the…"

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:19.620
Larry the Commercial Guy

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:23.690
Instead of looking for Larry in the movies,
you might be better off looking in the grocery

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:24.690
aisle.

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:28.110
Bektrom Foods, a company that makes Hamburger
Helper-style dinners and other shelf-stable

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:33.200
foods, licensed Larry's likeness for use on
a line of products sold in grocery and drugstores.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.160
The result of that deal has seen Larry show
up on a few dozen Bektrom items, including

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.510
Larry the Cable Guy Spicy Corn Muffin Mix
and Larry the Cable Guy Cheesy Tuna Dinner,

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.110
among many, many others.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:47.540
Meanwhile, a snack food company called Shearer's
has also paid Whitney for its Larry the Cable

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.770
Guy Caramel &amp; Peanuts Country Corn and a few
different kinds of Larry the Cable Guy Tater

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:56.160
chips, including, but not limited to, Tater
Salad, and Hollar-Peño Popper.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:00.150
Larry didn't stop there: he also sells a line
of kitchen knives, including a "Melon Cuttin'

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:04.550
Knife," a "Bonin' Knife," a "Slicin'" Knife,
and, of course, a "Tater Peeler."

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:09.119
Ironically — or maybe inevitably — Larry's
also been the longtime pitchman for Prilosec,

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:11.050
an over-the-counter medication to treat heartburn.

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:15.340
"'Cause it gives me a big fat zero heartburn,
woo hoo!"

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:17.280
He walked away from Only in America

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.010
In 2011, Larry starred in a History Channel
show called Only in America with Larry the

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:26.139
Cable Guy, which saw him travelling around
the country to discover all the wild, interesting

00:02:26.139 --> 00:02:27.730
stuff America has to offer.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:31.659
He visited Amish country, hunted snakes, and
tested lasers with the Army.

00:02:31.659 --> 00:02:33.459
"You could cook a pot pie with that."

00:02:33.459 --> 00:02:37.379
The show was a huge hit for History, but it
was abruptly canceled after three seasons

00:02:37.379 --> 00:02:41.209
— mainly because it's hard to make Only
in America with Larry the Cable Guy without

00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:42.540
Larry the Cable Guy.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:44.159
There were two reasons he quit.

00:02:44.159 --> 00:02:47.840
The first was an episode in which he had to
clean portable toilets at a music festival

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.930
in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.420
He explained to a reporter:

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.950
"I didn't want to do it.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:54.939
I mean, that was one of the nastiest things
on the planet."

00:02:54.939 --> 00:02:58.470
The other reason he walked away — as if
he needed one, was that the show required

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:00.019
him to be on the road so much.

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:03.400
That, combined with a career as a touring
stand-up comedian, pulled him away from his

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.439
family for as many as six days a week.

00:03:05.439 --> 00:03:09.599
He chose his family, but the result was showing
up on the small screen much less.

00:03:09.599 --> 00:03:11.169
He's still making movies

00:03:11.169 --> 00:03:14.819
While he's no longer starring in big-screen
fish-out-of-water comedies like Health Inspector

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:19.390
or Witless Protection, Whitney is still making
movies — just not ones you'll see in theaters.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:23.499
Instead, direct your attention to your favorite
streaming service, or the video rack at your

00:03:23.499 --> 00:03:24.910
local Target.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:28.860
Whitney took over for Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson
in Tooth Fairy 2 and for Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:30.370
in Jingle All the Way 2.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:35.249
He also reunited with his Blue Collar Comedy
Tour compatriot Jeff Foxworthy for the Netflix

00:03:35.249 --> 00:03:37.859
original We've Been Thinking.

00:03:37.859 --> 00:03:38.859
Larry the corporate guy

00:03:38.859 --> 00:03:43.120
It's a little-discussed but incredibly lucrative
side of professional comedy: well-known comedians

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:46.599
can get paid a fortune for "corporate gigs"
where they're hired to be the entertainment

00:03:46.599 --> 00:03:50.829
for a huge company's convention, annual meeting,
or managerial retreat.

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:54.510
Even comedians who aren't as popular as they
once were can pull in some serious cash on

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:55.530
this circuit.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:59.269
Larry the Cable Guy makes a lot of these corporate
appearances, and for his trouble, he's paid

00:03:59.269 --> 00:04:04.779
at least in the neighborhood of $150,000 to
$299,000—for each performance.

00:04:04.779 --> 00:04:08.779
If you're not seeing Larry at your local comedy
club, maybe that's because he's performing

00:04:08.779 --> 00:04:12.719
at the annual retreat for In-N-Out Burger's
board of directors.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:13.719
Larry the charity guy

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:18.080
Larry’s made millions off his act and licensing
deals — and he hasn't been shy about donating

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.880
that money to causes he believes in.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:24.010
In his hometown of Pawnee City, Nebraska,
he donated money to the city and his old high

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:25.010
school.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:28.670
He's also a major patron of the Arnold Palmer
Hospital for Children and its International

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:33.530
Hip Dysplasia Institute going back to 2007,
when his son, Wyatt Whitney, was born with

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:34.540
the disorder.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.760
Doctors there completely cured baby Wyatt
of the issue, and Larry quietly donated lots

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:42.790
of money to the medical complex through appearances
on celebrity editions of Are You Smarter Than

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:44.730
a Fifth Grader? and Family Feud.

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:49.900
In September 2010, he donated a whopping $5
million to the hospital, which how boasts

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:51.510
a Wyatt Whitney Wing.

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:55.700
Larry and his wife Cara also co-founded the
Git-R-Done Foundation, which gits-r-done,

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:59.010
charity-wise, for causes affecting veterans
and children.

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:02.480
Larry's actually making a huge difference
— you just might not have heard all about

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:03.480
it.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.120
What's next for Larry the Cable Guy

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:09.160
Because Larry the Cable Guy has become one
of the most memorable characters in comedy,

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:12.580
millions of fans don't really care that he's
not as hot as he once was.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:16.400
Plus, he's set to reprise his role as Mater
in the upcoming Cars 3.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:20.310
So even if you don't see Larry as much as
you used to, there's no question he'll still,

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:21.570
well, you know…

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:22.830
"Get er doneeee!"

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.010
Thanks for watching!

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.690
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:28.919
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love too!

